> **Why gathered.** Demand evidence that agents author *real governance documents* in UDON where
> structure and prose interleave at depth — and that they lean on `;` comments for conventions and
> section banners and on health/drain attribute tags for machine-legible status. Extract is the head
> (schema + conventions + spine); the full 489-line file continues the same pattern.


|process-map[asf-processes]
  :title The meta-processes of ASF, as a system
  :created 2026-07-07
  :version 0.0.1
  :status first-pass

  ; A MECE-ish list of the processes that run (or should run), in mild hierarchy. Correct the carve freely.

  ; Conventions:
    - Each process carries a `health` tag (from findings) and a `drain` tag.
    - `drain` values:
      | healing    (steady-state, self-clearing if given a trigger + "do-one-extra" rule)
      | task-force (a one-off is the right fit; a steady rhythm would mis-fit)
      | nil        (not a backlog-shaped process)

    - A `?` marks a genuinely unknown sub-process we'd have to design.
    - Signal-flow is noted per-item as fed-by / feeds, and drawn only for the
      core loop, where it clarifies the dynamics.

  |meta-meta-process[self-governance]
    :name How this map governs and evolves itself
    :source-sink participant-feedback

    Kept to a few imperatives on purpose:
    - Make it easy to follow the *right current* process, or to reach for the
      tool around it.
    - Make it just as easy to *evolve* a process — incrementally, or more
      fundamentally.
    - Every participant may give feedback and ideas on *any* process.
    - That participant feedback is the *only* source/sink point of the
      meta-process itself.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; THE SPINE -- cross-cutting, not a stage
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[spine]
    :name Decision-routing & stewardship
    :scope cross-cutting

    Every stall below reduces to a decision that never reached Joseph in
    actionable form; this is the parent, not a sibling (cluster 02's insight).

    |process[decision-surfacing]
      :name Decision surfacing
      :health broken
      :drain healing
      :example spikes/epistemic-target-ontology/

      Recognize a genuine-Joseph fork, assemble a real brief (reconstructed
      context + options + recommendation + honest uncertainty + the actual
      pointer), route it to a valve he can act from. JOSEPH-TODO catches under
      half (`<½`); the newer half leaks. Per-fork trigger + prune. The worked
      example that already exists is `spikes/epistemic-target-ontology/`.

    |process[coherence-stewardship]?
      :name Coherence stewardship (the domain-master role)
      :health absent
      :drain nil
      :design-unknown how it's instantiated across turnover

      Not a gatekeeper; a check on cross-process coherence who can say "hold that
      integration until the intro lands," "these two pull opposite ways — make
      them read each other first." A standing role, not a queue.

    |process[valve]
      :name The valve itself (JOSEPH-TODO)
      :health under-fed
      :drain healing

      The durable list of genuinely-his calls. Exists, well-designed,
      under-fed.

  ; ==========================================================================
  ; GENERATION (sources)
  ; ==========================================================================

  |cluster[generation]
    :name Generation (sources)

    |process[spike-lifecycle]
      :name Spike lifecycle
      :health healthy
      :drain nil
      :feeds [verification integration]

      Launch → derive → refute-verify → land self-contained at honest tier. It's
      a source, not a queue.


; […head extract ends at line 90 of 489 — same |process[slug]+:health/:drain+prose pattern continues…]
